    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3130" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκέων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουσα</span>,
		participial form, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>softly,
				silently</i>, fem. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκέουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.565
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.142
			</span></i>: dual. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκέοντε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.195
				</span></i>
			; also indecl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκέων δαίνυσθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.89
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				404
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθηναίη ἀκέων ἦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.22
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				8.459
			</span></i>.</div>
